From f2eedafa096e4999354e207dd28f5ef41ee67fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:35:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] feat(tools): resolve spindle tool assemblies to gauge
 length, cutting data and body

A stack of #3642 tool components, each with its port frames, cutting
point and revolved body, resolves by forward kinematics: the root MCS is
the identity, each child MCS sits on its parent's port, turned about the
mating Z and moved to its stickout. The result is moved so that the
cutting tip is the tool-frame origin. It gives the gauge length, the
cutting diameter and corner radius (a solid tool's own, or an insert's
from its seat point and nose), and the judged HolderProfile that the
collision laws read today. A plain collet chuck or Weldon holder and an
end mill give the same gauge length and bands as the library HolderRef.

Refused by name: the #3642 fit errors, a missing frame, an ambiguous or
taken port, a cycle, a bad parent, two roots or cutters, a non-finite
turn or stickout, a stickout off a plain or Weldon bore, an off-axis
body, and a body in the flutes. The lathe half stays on #3643.

Refs #3643

