From 8087437988b32fe132db75307a580c3d4621efc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:59:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(tools): a shank sits home only on a stated bore stop;
 pin the body union rules

Review findings of #4119:
- A solid tool on a plain or Weldon bore with no stickout now needs a
  bore stop that the parent's geometry states
  (ComponentGeometry::with_stop). The nose face is no home position. A
  stickout that pushes the shank past a stated stop is refused. The
  library holders state no bore depth, so they need a stated stickout.
- The Weldon equivalence pin runs at the true stickout (tool length
  less the stop depth), with the stop and with the same stickout stated.
- New pins for the union rules: overlap keeps the larger radius, a gap
  takes the smaller neighbour.
- to_tool names the node whose frame fails; a comment on the dropped
  display outline; the decision file is corrected.

Refs #3643

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
